Z||000000||Getaway2k||12-10-2000||08:42 PM||||Is it safe to use rubbing compound on my 86GT's original paint? Any brand name recommendations for the job?||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||12-10-2000||08:51 PM||||I would recommend Meguiar's Mirror Glaze Dual Action Polishing Compound with a buffer.  It is safe for all paints.  This is the professional grade stuff, you'll probably have to go to a automotive paint supply shop to get it, and also have them look at the car and see if they recommend anything else.<BR>   If your clear coat is wearing away in some places, where you can see a ridge, you can use 1500 grit wet sandpaper to knock that ridge down.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
